---
description: "Fix one cluster of confirmed quality issues, keep the offline gate green, report per-issue outcomes"
mode: subagent
model: "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"
tools: read, grep, bash, edit, write
tool_loop:
  max_rounds: 150
params:
  manifest: string
  guidance: string
system: "You are a careful, surgical fixer of confirmed code-quality issues. You make the minimal change each issue calls for, you keep behavior identical, and you keep the offline verification gate green. You never touch the quality store, never run git write commands, and never expand scope beyond the issues you were handed."
---
let issue_files = read({ path: manifest })?
let extra = guidance == "" ? "(none)" : guidance

import { FixReport } from "./quality.thetalib"

let r: FixReport = @`FIX TASK — resolve this cluster of confirmed code-quality issues.

Issue files, one per line — read each fully; they carry the evidence and a
non-binding direction:
${issue_files}

Rules:
- Each issue's lens: frontmatter selects the per-lens rules below.
- Re-verify each issue against the CURRENT code before touching anything (code
  may have moved since filing). If it no longer reproduces, skip it and say why.
- A fix is the minimal change that removes the crufted code or vestige. Preserve
  behavior. No drive-by refactors, no unrelated edits, no formatting sweeps.
  Follow docs/STYLE.md where it applies.
- Deleting production code may orphan tests that existed only to exercise the
  deleted cruft: delete those tests with it and say so in your notes, per issue.
  Never weaken or delete an assertion that guards live behavior.
- Never edit anything under quality/. Never run git commands that change state
  (add, commit, restore, checkout, stash) — the orchestrator owns git and the
  store. Reading git history is fine.

- Verification, after all edits: run, as ONE bash command, exactly
  "unset PI_THETA_SUBAGENT_ROOT PI_THETA_SUBAGENT_ROOT_WINNER PI_THETA_PARAMS PI_THETA_PARAMS_FILE PI_THETA_SUBAGENT_INVOKE_DEPTH PI_THETA_SUBAGENT_CALLABLE_HASHES PI_THETA_SUBAGENT_PARENT_PID; npx tsc --noEmit && npm test"
  (use a generous bash timeout, e.g. 2400 seconds — the suite is large). The
  unset prefix is required because you run inside a subagent whose environment
  carries the wrapper's control plane, and the suite spawns real child pi
  processes that would otherwise inherit and legitimately re-authenticate that
  foreign plane, turning unrelated tests fail-closed red (bug 0474). Both
  must pass. If red, repair your own change, or back the offending edit out by
  editing the code back to its original text, and mark that issue skipped.

Per-lens rules — apply per issue, by its lens: frontmatter:
- lens: D2 (cruft in src/): as today — minimal removal of the crufted code or
  vestige, behavior preserved. Deleting production code may orphan tests that
  existed only to exercise the deleted cruft: delete those tests with it and
  say so in your notes, per issue. Never weaken or delete an assertion that
  guards live behavior.
- lens: D7 (test quality in tests/): remove the smell WITHOUT weakening the
  suite. A vacuous assertion is replaced by a real observable (system notes,
  userTexts/toolCalls, recorded double state — never a bare
  resolves.toBeDefined and never a stochastic-text sentinel); a test is
  deleted only if it verifies nothing AND nothing cites it (grep
  docs/reference/coverage-matrix.md, docs/bugs/, and test files for its name
  first). Dedupe boilerplate into tests/helpers/ — extend an existing helper
  before adding a new one. If a change renames or merges a test cited by
  coverage-matrix.md or a bug doc's witness list, re-point that citation in
  the same change. Never touch production src/ for a D7 issue.

Guidance from a previous rejected attempt — address it explicitly if present:
${extra}

When done, reply with the requested schema:
- fixed: issue file BASENAMES (e.g. PTQ-0007-some-slug.md) fully fixed with the
  gate green
- skipped: issue file basenames not fixed
- notes: one line per issue — what was done, or why it was skipped.`?
r
